// Reset value of a cell's packed state: cid = identity's id, whole = 1,
// everything else 0.
// Layout {cid, active, whole, defect, ptr, grown, unrooted, busy} means
// cid sits at bit (6 + PTR_W) and whole at (4 + PTR_W) -- a fixed `<< 7`
// is only correct when PTR_W == 1, and getting it wrong leaves the cid's
// top bits as X (and `x + delta` stays X).
// one entry per cell, SNOW_PE_STW bits each (the RTL reads entry CELL
// with `[CELL*SNOW_PE_STW +: SNOW_PE_STW]`)
localparam integer SNOW_LAT_PE_RST_VEC [0:35] = '{4224, 1152, 13440, 7296, 13952, 7808, 14464, 8320, 14976, 8832, 4736, 1664, 3200, 128, 11392, 5248, 11904, 5760, 12416, 6272, 12928, 6784, 3712, 640, 2176, 128, 9344, 128, 9856, 128, 10368, 128, 10880, 128, 2688, 128};

// ---- the whole bank's power-up value, ONE entry per ADDRESS ----------
// The one-datapath-per-slot array cannot preset a cell from its own
// `always` block with a compile-time address (the address is `phase`-
// dependent), and a reset branch that walks the contexts makes Vivado see
// a VARIABLE-address write racing the commit write -- measured: 50x
// `[Synth 8-6859] multi-driven net on pin Q ... 2nd driver 'GND'` plus
// `8-6858 constant driver PRESERVED, other driver ignored` on `bank_reg[*][*]`,
// which both zeroes live state and folds the datapath away (the same
// design reported 203 LUT / 962 FF / 435 MHz -- a netlist that is NOT the
// RTL that was verified line by line).
//
// So the preset is emitted as a FULL MEMORY IMAGE and applied by the one
// `initial` loop the array already had.  Every address then has exactly
// one constant driver, the clocked block is the only other driver, and
// `reset` no longer touches the bank at all.
